«
@@ DMOWalk — demo of the Probability section: two random walks in the
@@ plane, 200 steps each, in uniformly random directions, with the same
@@ mean step length 3. Left, steps drawn from Expon (λ = 1/3): a Brownian
@@ walk, the drunkard's walk. Right, steps drawn from Pareto, of exponent
@@ α = 1.2 or the one given on the stack (1 < α ≤ 3), with xm = 3(α-1)/α:
@@ for α < 2 the variance is infinite, a Lévy flight, clusters of short
@@ steps joined by rare long jumps. Each walk is scaled to its own
@@ panel; the start is marked by a square. Returns, for each walk, the
@@ share of the whole path taken by its longest step.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @ The exponent, if given; any other object is left alone
  0
  If Depth 1 > Then Drop Dup TypeName End
  → dmwty
  «
  1.2
  If dmwty "decimal" == dmwty "integer" == Or dmwty "fraction" == Or Then
    Over Dup 1 > Swap 3 ≤ And
    If Then Drop End
  End
  Dup 1 - 3 * Over /
  → dmwal dmwxm
  «
  ClearLCD
  { #199d #20d } { #199d #239d } DrawLine
  "Brownian: Expon steps" { #4d #2d 0 true false } DrawText
  "Lévy: Pareto α=" dmwal →Text + { #204d #2d 0 true false } DrawText
  @ Panel 1, the Brownian walk; panel 2, the Lévy flight
  1 2 For dmwh
    @ The walk: 201 points, the longest step, the length of the path
    0 0 0 0
    → dmwx dmwy dmwm dmws
    «
      0 0 R→C
      1 200 For dmwi
        If dmwh 1 == Then 1 3 / ⓁExponRand Else dmwxm dmwal ⓁParetoRand End
        RAND 360 * 1_° *
        → dmwr dmwt
        «
          dmwx dmwr dmwt Cos * + 'dmwx' Sto
          dmwy dmwr dmwt Sin * + 'dmwy' Sto
          dmwm dmwr Max 'dmwm' Sto
          dmws dmwr + 'dmws' Sto
          dmwx dmwy R→C
        »
      Next
      201 →List
      dmwm dmws /
    »
    → dmwp dmwq
    «
      @ The bounding box, then the scale and centre of the panel
      dmwp 1 Get Re Dup dmwp 1 Get Im Dup
      → dmwx0 dmwx1 dmwy0 dmwy1
      «
        1 201 For dmwi
          dmwp dmwi Get
          → dmwz
          «
            dmwx0 dmwz Re Min 'dmwx0' Sto
            dmwx1 dmwz Re Max 'dmwx1' Sto
            dmwy0 dmwz Im Min 'dmwy0' Sto
            dmwy1 dmwz Im Max 'dmwy1' Sto
          »
        Next
        186 dmwx1 dmwx0 - / 186 dmwy1 dmwy0 - / Min
        dmwx0 dmwx1 + 2 / dmwy0 dmwy1 + 2 /
        dmwh 1 - 200 * 100 +
        → dmwk dmwxc dmwyc dmwc
        «
          @ Every point to a pixel { #x #y }
          1 201 For dmwi
            dmwp dmwi Get
            → dmwz
            «
              dmwc dmwz Re dmwxc - dmwk * + IP R→I R→B
              122 dmwz Im dmwyc - dmwk * - IP R→I R→B
              2 →List
            »
          Next
          201 →List
          → dmwpx
          «
            2 201 For dmwi
              dmwpx dmwi 1 - Get dmwpx dmwi Get DrawLine
            Next
            @ The start, a small square
            dmwpx 1 Get 1 Get B→R dmwpx 1 Get 2 Get B→R
            → dmwu dmwv
            «
              dmwu 3 - R→B dmwv 3 - R→B 2 →List
              dmwu 3 + R→B dmwv 3 - R→B 2 →List
              dmwu 3 + R→B dmwv 3 + R→B 2 →List
              dmwu 3 - R→B dmwv 3 + R→B 2 →List
              → dmwa dmwb dmwe dmwf
              «
                dmwa dmwb DrawLine dmwb dmwe DrawLine
                dmwe dmwf DrawLine dmwf dmwa DrawLine
              »
            »
            "longest step " dmwq 100 * IP R→I →Text + "%" +
            dmwh 1 - 200 * 4 + R→B #220d 2 →List { 0 true false } + DrawText
            dmwq 3 RND
          »
        »
      »
    »
  Next
  2 →List "longest step / path" →Tag
  »
  »
»
